WEBVTT

00:05.060 --> 00:10.490
<i>When I lost my parents, my grandmother 
who lived in the countryside took me in.</i>

00:11.380 --> 00:15.620
<i>The bag I clutched held 
everything I had in the world.</i>

00:19.450 --> 00:22.000
<i>My grandmother, Tae, hugged me.</i>

00:23.030 --> 00:26.730
<i>Ever since that moment, 
I've been my grandma's girl.</i>

00:28.150 --> 00:31.640
<i>My life with my grandmother 
wasn't full of luxury,</i>

00:32.790 --> 00:35.720
<i>but those were peaceful, gentle days.</i>

00:36.820 --> 00:37.740
<i>However...</i>

00:39.290 --> 00:41.580
<i>My clothes were all either 
made by my grandmother</i>

00:41.580 --> 00:43.900
<i>or bought on sale at a steep discount,</i>

00:44.360 --> 00:47.650
<i>so the other students in 
my class made fun of me.</i>

00:47.650 --> 00:50.670
You always wear the same clothes.

00:51.290 --> 00:53.410
Have you ever washed them?

00:57.160 --> 01:01.550
Everyone, make sure to bring a dust rag 
on the day of our school-wide cleaning!

01:07.270 --> 01:11.500
I've sewn plenty of them, so share 
some with the other children, too.

01:15.550 --> 01:17.430
Oh, I forgot.

01:19.110 --> 01:20.900
Can someone lend me a dust rag?

01:22.190 --> 01:23.880
U-Um...

01:25.070 --> 01:28.610
I have extra. You can use one.

01:28.610 --> 01:30.550
Uh, okay...

01:32.380 --> 01:37.200
Seriously? That's the same material as 
the clothes you're wearing right now.

01:37.200 --> 01:40.050
You've been wearing rags this whole time.

01:42.950 --> 01:45.020
It smells weird, too.

01:46.620 --> 01:48.560
Pass! Pass!

01:52.600 --> 01:54.090
Don't!

01:54.760 --> 01:57.350
You're right! It reeks of old people smell.

01:58.580 --> 01:59.600
Give it back!

01:59.600 --> 02:02.580
Stop it. I feel bad for her.

02:10.610 --> 02:12.110
Give it back!

02:12.110 --> 02:14.110
<b>Meeting Room</b>

02:12.910 --> 02:16.270
Manami got in a fight?

02:16.600 --> 02:20.210
The other child's parents are very angry.

02:20.210 --> 02:24.540
Uname-san, could you apologize as soon 
as possible to calm the situation?

02:25.440 --> 02:29.380
But Manami wouldn't be violent 
without a good reason.

02:29.380 --> 02:30.530
There must be some misundersta—

02:30.530 --> 02:34.630
Are you saying there's a problem 
with the way I manage my class?

02:37.390 --> 02:38.930
But...

02:40.440 --> 02:42.990
Manami-san being such a troublemaker

02:42.990 --> 02:46.400
suggests that the problem lies 
squarely at home. Don't you think?

02:59.620 --> 03:04.410
<b>Mysterious Disappearances</b>

02:59.620 --> 03:04.410
<b>Mysterious Disappearances</b>

04:24.990 --> 04:27.000
<b>KISARAGI</b>

04:25.660 --> 04:32.540
<b>Horns, Bullying, and a Hair Ornament</b>

04:25.660 --> 04:32.540
<b>Horns, Bullying, and a Hair Ornament</b>

04:27.950 --> 04:30.750
Hitting the jackpot on your 
first day of infiltration...

04:30.750 --> 04:32.880
I'd expect no less of you, Sumireko-san.

04:32.880 --> 04:36.880
I didn't ask for your opinion. 
What happened to my clothes?

04:36.880 --> 04:41.390
I sent them to be cleaned, along 
with your drool-covered uniform.

04:41.850 --> 04:43.610
More importantly, what do you think?

04:43.610 --> 04:46.890
Were you able to determine anything
after seeing the dribblers in person?

04:47.220 --> 04:51.650
Only that whoever diagnosed 
that as a disease has to be blind.

04:52.000 --> 04:54.790
It's something else. Something different.

04:54.790 --> 04:57.530
The three who collapsed are unhurt, right?

04:57.530 --> 05:02.030
When the teachers took them outside, 
all three regained consciousness.

05:02.440 --> 05:06.430
Good. Very good.
That can't be explained by nature.

05:07.690 --> 05:09.670
You're certainly in a good mood.

05:09.670 --> 05:11.420
Well, of course I am.

05:12.380 --> 05:15.040
At last, I've found another Curiosity.

05:15.720 --> 05:16.920
It won't get away.

05:19.210 --> 05:22.040
You saw Markers appear 
when they collapsed, right?

05:22.430 --> 05:23.840
Yes.

05:23.840 --> 05:26.430
But I couldn't do anything.

05:27.050 --> 05:31.190
It's all right, Oto. Your friends 
collapsed right in front of you.

05:31.530 --> 05:34.090
As long as you're okay, 
that's all that matters to me.

05:34.880 --> 05:36.070
Ren-nii...

05:37.160 --> 05:40.310
I wouldn't mind if you were 
a little worried for me, too.

05:41.080 --> 05:42.820
Of course I am.

05:42.820 --> 05:44.260
Oto comes first, though.

05:44.260 --> 05:46.330
I'm honored to hear it.

05:48.630 --> 05:52.210
I think we can safely say that a 
Curiosity is present at that school.

05:52.620 --> 05:55.210
The next step is to capture it.

05:55.210 --> 05:56.750
Capture it?

05:58.300 --> 06:01.390
A philosopher of the Meiji Era, Inoue Enryo,

06:00.000 --> 06:01.590
<b>\hInoue Enryo\h</b>

06:01.390 --> 06:03.820
wrote in his <i>Lectures on Youkai</i>

06:02.380 --> 06:03.710
<b>\h\hLectures on Youkai\h\h</b>

06:03.470 --> 06:04.670
<b>Youkai</b>

06:03.470 --> 06:04.670
<b>Youkai</b>

06:03.820 --> 06:06.960
that youkai are divided into 
"true mysteries" and "false mysteries."

06:04.720 --> 06:06.850
<b>True
Mysteries</b>

06:04.720 --> 06:06.850
<b>True
Mysteries</b>

06:04.720 --> 06:06.850
<b>False
Mysteries</b>

06:04.720 --> 06:06.850
<b>False
Mysteries</b>

06:06.840 --> 06:08.640
<b>False
Mysteries</b>

06:06.840 --> 06:08.640
<b>False
Mysteries</b>

06:07.420 --> 06:10.880
False mysteries are fictions born of 
things like fear or misunderstanding.

06:11.480 --> 06:14.020
<b>False
Mysteries</b>

06:11.480 --> 06:14.020
<b>False
Mysteries</b>

06:11.480 --> 06:14.020
<b>True
Mysteries</b>

06:11.480 --> 06:14.020
<b>True
Mysteries</b>

06:11.960 --> 06:16.260
In contrast, true mysteries are 
indicative of real anomalous phenomena.

06:16.610 --> 06:18.360
<b>True
Mysteries</b>

06:16.610 --> 06:18.360
<b>True
Mysteries</b>

06:17.420 --> 06:21.370
True mysteries are further divided into 
"genuine mysteries" and "reputed mysteries."

06:18.440 --> 06:22.110
<b>Genuine
Mysteries</b>

06:18.440 --> 06:22.110
<b>Genuine
Mysteries</b>

06:18.440 --> 06:22.110
<b>Reputed
Mysteries</b>

06:18.440 --> 06:22.110
<b>Reputed
Mysteries</b>

06:21.370 --> 06:25.870
Anomalous phenomena that can be verified 
in some way are called reputed mysteries.

06:26.650 --> 06:32.120
And truly anomalous phenomena that science 
can't explain are genuine mysteries.

06:32.520 --> 06:36.880
But Enryo's definition of genuine mysteries 
applies to all laws of nature.

06:36.880 --> 06:40.250
In a way, it's the exact 
opposite of Curiosities.

06:37.040 --> 06:40.250
<b>Wood</b>

06:37.040 --> 06:40.250
<b>Fire</b>

06:37.040 --> 06:40.250
<b>Earth</b>

06:37.040 --> 06:40.250
<b>Metal</b>

06:37.040 --> 06:40.250
<b>Water</b>

06:40.750 --> 06:43.980
It's just the sort of romantic interpretation 
a philosopher would make, isn't it?

06:44.750 --> 06:47.260
But unfortunately, I'm not Enryo.

06:47.260 --> 06:49.850
<b>Genuine Mysteries</b>

06:47.260 --> 06:49.850
<b>Genuine Mysteries</b>

06:47.260 --> 06:50.020
My definition of genuine 
mysteries is more literal.

06:50.020 --> 06:52.020
They are genuine Curiosities.

06:50.180 --> 06:52.020
<b>Genuine Curiosities</b>

06:50.180 --> 06:52.020
<b>Genuine Curiosities</b>

06:52.350 --> 06:53.700
I see.

06:53.700 --> 06:57.740
Genuine mysteries are very rare, 
so I have an idea of what it could be.

06:58.380 --> 07:03.280
You do? In that case, my girls' school 
infiltration mission has come to an end.

07:04.780 --> 07:06.190
What are you talking about?

07:06.190 --> 07:06.970
Huh?

07:08.280 --> 07:12.010
I'll be needing you to go 
to school tomorrow, too.

07:12.010 --> 07:12.910
What?!

07:12.910 --> 07:15.830
Oto, you want to save your friends, don't you?

07:16.500 --> 07:17.790
Yes.

07:17.790 --> 07:20.430
Then please leave everything to me.

07:24.880 --> 07:27.050
Good day to you, Sensei!

07:27.050 --> 07:28.540
Good day to you!

07:28.540 --> 07:30.650
Go straight home, all right?

07:32.060 --> 07:33.060
<b>In Use by the
Apartment Wife</b>

07:33.050 --> 07:34.050
<b>Wannabe</b>

07:33.050 --> 07:34.050
<b>Caterpillar
Brows</b>

07:34.060 --> 07:38.350
This is inhumane! I don't wanna 
eat lunch in the bathroom anymore!

07:38.350 --> 07:41.820
So why have I been shut in 
a cubicle again? Damn it!

07:44.390 --> 07:46.450
Wait there! I'll get the door open!

07:47.320 --> 07:50.960
Flower spikes on the top, too? How awful!

07:51.750 --> 07:54.580
It's all right! I'll get you out of there!

07:56.730 --> 07:58.690
Wakazukuri-san?

07:59.080 --> 08:01.110
Uname-sensei...

08:04.460 --> 08:06.260
You're all right now.

08:06.260 --> 08:08.090
Thank you.

08:08.090 --> 08:11.230
Wakazukuri-san, I really do think you're...

08:11.950 --> 08:14.100
I wanted to believe that I wasn't.

08:14.640 --> 08:17.120
I thought if I said, "I'm not being bullied,"

08:17.120 --> 08:21.670
and didn't acknowledge it, 
then it wouldn't really be bullying.

08:21.670 --> 08:27.450
And I figured that telling you 
wouldn't change anything anyway.

08:29.240 --> 08:31.210
This won't work after all.

08:31.210 --> 08:33.610
Targeting the perpetrators 
isn't enough to end it.

08:33.610 --> 08:35.990
I need to change my approach.

08:36.390 --> 08:39.000
The victims need time away from school, too.

08:39.000 --> 08:42.190
I'll give you the excuse you need to rest.

08:45.750 --> 08:47.790
The shadow shrank?

08:53.720 --> 08:56.600
Good day to you. I'm delighted 
to make your acquaintance.

08:59.790 --> 09:02.330
From now on, licking the floor is forbidden.

09:02.330 --> 09:03.870
O-Okay...

09:03.870 --> 09:05.820
Huh? Why is there a boy here?

09:05.820 --> 09:07.610
And who is that child?

09:08.040 --> 09:11.110
What is this? Who are you two?

09:11.750 --> 09:15.360
I'm simply the guardian 
of one of the students here.

09:15.360 --> 09:19.660
And she's a curvy woman with 
fluffy caterpillar eyebrows.

09:20.030 --> 09:22.470
Who are you calling curvy with 
fluffy caterpillar eyebrows?

09:24.020 --> 09:27.720
Look the other way! 
Why are you staring like that?

09:27.720 --> 09:29.300
Wakazukuri-san?

09:29.300 --> 09:32.380
Were you that child earlier, too?

09:33.340 --> 09:37.950
More importantly... Uname-sensei, 
you're the one behind the dribblers?

09:39.040 --> 09:40.450
Ushi-oni.

09:39.060 --> 09:40.890
<b>\hUshi-oni\h</b>

09:41.820 --> 09:43.400
Most of the time in folklore,

09:43.750 --> 09:50.400
it's depicted as a cruel monster 
that likes to kill and eat humans.

09:50.400 --> 09:55.410
The bull-headed spider from the picture scroll
<i>Hyakkai Zukan</i> is the most well-known,

09:55.720 --> 09:58.310
but it's unusual because its 
appearance and personality

09:58.310 --> 10:00.500
vary greatly depending on the folk tale.

10:01.160 --> 10:05.500
When an ushi-oni licks a person's shadow, 
they suddenly begin drooling,

10:05.500 --> 10:09.070
their body grows hot, as if it's burning, 
and eventually, they die.

10:09.070 --> 10:10.670
That's what the folk tales say.

10:11.380 --> 10:13.900
Don't you think it sounds 
a lot like the dribblers?

10:14.350 --> 10:17.470
And when I asked Tama-chan, 
the queen of gossip here...

10:18.930 --> 10:21.480
The dribblers?

10:21.480 --> 10:25.440
I think a lot of them were students who 
had gotten involved in some sort of fight.

10:26.680 --> 10:30.590
Given these points, I built 
a very rough hypothesis.

10:30.590 --> 10:31.900
Namely...

10:31.900 --> 10:36.200
that someone was borrowing the power 
of the ushi-oni to nip bullying in the bud.

10:36.820 --> 10:40.470
Which is why we set a trap 
with a bullying victim as the bait.

10:43.190 --> 10:44.710
Huh? What are you doing?

10:47.210 --> 10:48.210
Don't...

10:48.210 --> 10:49.680
Don't!

10:52.880 --> 10:54.260
Stop it!

10:54.720 --> 10:57.720
Stop! Please don't smell me!

10:57.720 --> 11:01.140
I see. So this is the cause.

11:03.290 --> 11:07.070
That hair ornament. 
If you'll just give that up,

11:07.070 --> 11:08.730
everything will be resolv—

11:12.550 --> 11:13.990
He's weaker than he seems!

11:15.060 --> 11:17.490
Why would you get in your teacher's way?

11:17.860 --> 11:19.490
Please calm down.

11:19.490 --> 11:23.930
You want to put an end to bullying, right?

11:23.930 --> 11:28.820
But what's the point if you have 
to hurt your students to do it?

11:30.550 --> 11:32.130
Please, Sensei.

11:32.480 --> 11:34.600
Please give us the ornament.

11:34.600 --> 11:38.760
Why not work with your students over time, 
and put an end to bullying for real?

11:41.700 --> 11:43.270
Wakazukuri-san...

11:46.030 --> 11:47.210
All right.

11:47.520 --> 11:49.740
I just need to give you this hair ornament?

11:51.180 --> 11:53.280
It's just as you say.

11:54.780 --> 12:00.060
But why do people have to say that getting 
rid of bullying isn't a simple thing?

12:00.060 --> 12:04.320
The children being bullied right now 
can't afford to sit around and wait.

12:05.790 --> 12:07.660
No! Sumireko-san!

12:22.470 --> 12:23.640
Sumireko-san!

12:30.920 --> 12:34.090
Stones drift. Leaves sink.

12:34.520 --> 12:37.570
Horses moo. Cows neigh.

12:38.470 --> 12:41.870
Stones drift. Leaves sink.

12:41.870 --> 12:44.780
Horses moo. Cows neigh.

12:44.780 --> 12:47.700
Adashino-kun?

12:47.700 --> 12:51.080
Sumireko-san. I see you've come to.

12:51.080 --> 12:54.540
I'm sorry. This is all my 
fault for misjudging her.

12:54.540 --> 12:57.170
Adashino-kun, your injuries...

12:57.520 --> 12:58.800
Please get away from here.

12:58.800 --> 13:00.050
Hey...

13:00.050 --> 13:02.380
Let's meet again at the bookshop.

13:02.380 --> 13:04.750
A lot of new volumes 
are coming out tomorrow.

13:07.700 --> 13:09.480
I have a favor to ask.

13:09.480 --> 13:13.980
If I don't return, please 
look after Oto for me.

13:14.630 --> 13:16.070
What? Wait!

13:26.390 --> 13:27.810
Manami-chan.

13:29.550 --> 13:34.260
I'm sorry the only family 
you have is your grandma.

13:44.570 --> 13:47.360
Manami-chan, hold out your hand.

13:50.420 --> 13:55.230
This is a precious amulet that's been 
passed down in our family for generations.

13:55.640 --> 13:58.630
It will protect you, no matter what.

13:59.230 --> 14:01.360
Now, let's go home.

14:03.720 --> 14:08.240
<i>The bullying that I suffered resulted 
in my grandma getting bullied, too.</i>

14:08.780 --> 14:11.250
<i>Adults bully each other, just like kids do.</i>

14:11.700 --> 14:14.100
<i>I'm going to create a world with no bullying!</i>

14:17.960 --> 14:19.000
Ow.

14:19.900 --> 14:22.260
I've quelled the fire.

14:22.260 --> 14:24.710
The inverse phrases of Ushimarobi.

14:24.710 --> 14:27.390
"Stones drift. Leaves sink."

14:28.350 --> 14:33.770
Folklore says that repeating inverse phrases 
is one method of counteracting an ushi-oni.

14:33.770 --> 14:36.150
It's because she tried to take my amulet!

14:36.150 --> 14:37.980
The precious keepsake my grandma left me!

14:37.980 --> 14:41.030
Amulet? What are you talking about?

14:41.030 --> 14:42.910
That's a curse.

14:44.240 --> 14:47.140
It's a relic known as the Ushinotama—

14:45.570 --> 14:48.450
<b>Ushinotama</b>

14:47.140 --> 14:49.160
a fragment of an ushi-oni.

14:49.160 --> 14:53.540
Your ancestors must have come from 
a family whose totem was the ushi-oni.

14:54.030 --> 14:57.670
But as the generations passed, 
those teachings faded,

14:58.030 --> 15:01.670
and now, it's seen as no more 
than a simple protective amulet.

15:01.990 --> 15:04.720
It's likely that your name, Uname,

15:04.720 --> 15:06.500
was changed to a homophone of what it was.

15:06.930 --> 15:09.970
<b>Uname</b>

15:07.250 --> 15:11.930
Your real name would be written with the 
characters for "female cow," also read "Uname."

15:10.380 --> 15:11.930
<b>Uname</b>

15:11.930 --> 15:13.180
A curse?

15:13.180 --> 15:14.520
Yes.

15:14.520 --> 15:16.940
And curses always come home to roost.

15:17.640 --> 15:22.760
The limbic system, which manages our 
instincts, has no concept of "subject."

15:19.230 --> 15:22.940
<b></b>Neocortex

15:19.230 --> 15:22.940
<b></b>Limbic System

15:19.230 --> 15:22.940
<b></b>Thalamus

15:19.230 --> 15:22.940
<b></b>Brain Stem

15:19.230 --> 15:22.940
<b></b>Cerebellum

15:20.690 --> 15:21.650
<b>Subject</b>

15:21.360 --> 15:22.310
<b>Subject</b>

15:21.940 --> 15:22.850
<b>Subject</b>

15:22.760 --> 15:26.580
So when we feel negative 
emotions toward others,

15:25.490 --> 15:27.190
<b>Self</b>

15:25.490 --> 15:27.190
<b>Others</b>

15:26.580 --> 15:29.180
our brains can't distinguish 
between them and ourselves.

15:29.030 --> 15:29.950
<b></b>Neocortex

15:29.030 --> 15:29.950
<b></b>Limbic System

15:29.030 --> 15:29.950
<b></b>Thalamus

15:29.030 --> 15:29.950
<b></b>Brain Stem

15:29.030 --> 15:29.950
<b></b>Cerebellum

15:30.320 --> 15:34.800
Cursing another curses oneself 
at the same time.

15:35.460 --> 15:40.580
That old saying, "If you curse someone, 
then dig two graves," has some truth to it.

15:42.500 --> 15:43.590
I'm begging you.

15:43.590 --> 15:45.760
Please give that to me.

15:46.150 --> 15:49.090
I need it to send my little sister home.

15:49.090 --> 15:52.820
With this, I can create 
a world with no bullying!

15:52.820 --> 15:56.100
And if I can do that, 
I don't care what happens to me!

15:56.100 --> 15:59.170
You don't even allow friends 
to goof around with each other.

15:59.710 --> 16:03.730
Is that really the world you're wishing for?

16:04.340 --> 16:08.240
"We were just goofing around," 
"I didn't mean it"...

16:08.750 --> 16:11.490
Those are the kinds of things 
that bullies always say!

16:11.920 --> 16:14.330
It seems we can't resolve this peacefully.

16:14.330 --> 16:17.140
That's a shame. It really is.

16:18.650 --> 16:20.750
I didn't want to do this,

16:21.060 --> 16:23.450
but I can't leave you to your own devices.

16:35.100 --> 16:39.390
The truth is, I do approve 
of your convictions.

16:40.110 --> 16:42.100
You are a kind person.

16:42.680 --> 16:43.520
Back then,

16:44.700 --> 16:47.950
if someone like you had been there with us,

16:50.030 --> 16:53.840
then maybe my sister and I 
wouldn't have ended up like this.

16:56.040 --> 16:58.490
But no matter what I do,

16:58.490 --> 17:02.800
I keep thinking about the feelings of those 
who have been excluded from the world.

17:10.170 --> 17:12.460
Poor Dust Rag.

17:12.460 --> 17:14.850
Stop. You shouldn't laugh.

17:21.110 --> 17:22.310
Oh, I'm sorry.

17:22.310 --> 17:25.570
I dropped your lunch.

17:25.570 --> 17:28.580
Sorry, but could you eat 
that off the floor for us?

17:32.940 --> 17:34.820
She's really eating it!

17:34.820 --> 17:36.750
Trust Dust Rag to clean up!

17:40.750 --> 17:44.940
Manami-chan, I know that you're a kind girl.

17:45.870 --> 17:49.030
You're my granddaughter, 
and I'm proud of you.

17:53.740 --> 17:56.740
<i>Grandma, I'm sorry.</i>

18:07.180 --> 18:09.110
Are you all right, Adashino-kun?

18:09.110 --> 18:11.920
Sumireko-san...

18:12.810 --> 18:15.380
Did you do this?

18:15.380 --> 18:18.370
I just gave it a little push.

18:18.370 --> 18:20.470
Will she be all right?

18:20.470 --> 18:22.860
It's karma.

18:23.280 --> 18:27.980
If she's killed someone with the Curiosity, 
then she won't live, either.

18:28.910 --> 18:31.030
Then she'll be all right.

18:31.030 --> 18:34.090
Uname-sensei isn't the kind 
of person who'd kill anyone.

18:34.090 --> 18:37.640
Seriously? You forget things 
really fast, don't you, Eyebrows?

18:38.060 --> 18:41.660
By the way, it seems like 
all of my injuries are gone.

18:41.660 --> 18:43.390
What's going on here?

18:43.390 --> 18:47.050
The Curse of Youth is similar to shape-memory.

18:47.050 --> 18:49.880
You'll recover from a certain level of injury.

18:49.880 --> 18:53.040
I'm turning more and more 
into a monster myself.

18:54.000 --> 18:55.210
It's kinda freaky.

18:55.210 --> 18:56.280
Sumireko-san...

18:56.280 --> 18:58.440
Why didn't you run away?

18:58.440 --> 19:00.400
I made a cool exit and everything.

19:00.400 --> 19:01.720
Don't be ridiculous.

19:02.160 --> 19:03.880
And don't underestimate me.

19:03.880 --> 19:05.490
I'm a novelist, you know.

19:05.850 --> 19:08.920
How could I leave without knowing the ending?

19:09.370 --> 19:13.540
Please. You look like a gacha game 
character who's taken heavy damage.

19:13.540 --> 19:14.920
Ren-nii!

19:14.920 --> 19:16.320
Oto-chan!

19:16.320 --> 19:17.680
Your brother is all ri—

19:18.540 --> 19:20.930
<i>Ren-nii, your eyes! Are you okay?</i>

19:20.930 --> 19:23.950
<i>I'm sorry. The only option I had was to See.</i>

19:24.760 --> 19:27.290
<i>Now the talisman is just an empty shell.</i>

19:28.600 --> 19:31.230
<i>You're more important than a ticket, Ren-nii!</i>

19:31.230 --> 19:33.440
<i>Please don't push yourself so hard!</i>

19:38.500 --> 19:42.400
Shall we head back, Adashino-kun? 
It's time for the students to go home.

19:44.450 --> 19:46.460
<b>Takamanohara Hospital</b>

19:53.400 --> 19:56.720
The dribbler incidents have been 
resolved, so that's case closed.

19:54.110 --> 19:55.990
Good day to you, Sensei!

19:57.340 --> 19:58.870
You three...

19:57.340 --> 20:00.470
Thank you for your help, Sumireko-san.

20:00.470 --> 20:03.290
So did the ushi-oni disappear?

20:01.300 --> 20:03.290
We came to see how you were doing.

20:03.290 --> 20:05.980
Oh, right. I didn't tell you.

20:03.290 --> 20:05.980
Are the three of you all right now?

20:06.340 --> 20:08.720
We wanted to go back to 
school as soon as possible.

20:06.790 --> 20:11.250
Sorry. That wasn't an ushi-oni.

20:08.730 --> 20:13.360
We wanted to apologize to Wakazukuri-senpai 
for all the trouble we caused.

20:11.630 --> 20:13.360
It was something way more dangerous.

20:13.360 --> 20:14.480
What?

20:13.360 --> 20:15.540
It's just like you said, Sensei.

20:14.480 --> 20:19.180
I did think that it was way too brutal 
to be your average ushi-oni. Ha ha ha!

20:15.540 --> 20:18.360
We shouldn't make anyone do 
things they don't want to do.

20:19.180 --> 20:21.330
"Ha ha ha"? You little...

20:22.970 --> 20:25.870
Then what on earth was it?

20:26.550 --> 20:28.000
The Chinrinki.

20:26.660 --> 20:32.080
<b>\h\hChinrinki\h\h</b>

20:28.000 --> 20:32.860
It was a fierce god with eight heads, 
winged and red in color.

20:32.860 --> 20:34.890
When the Yamato court defeated the Chinrinki,

20:34.890 --> 20:38.510
fragments of it became ushi-oni. 
That's what people say.

20:38.980 --> 20:42.140
That teacher must have been 
weakening the curse's true power

20:42.140 --> 20:44.800
by reciting inverse phrases.

20:46.230 --> 20:49.120
That's why I misread 
the cause of the incidents.

20:49.470 --> 20:51.270
This is all just speculation, though.

20:52.090 --> 20:55.530
That teacher's powers, 
the Curiosity in question...

20:55.530 --> 20:57.730
Both have been lost, you see.

21:05.990 --> 21:07.460
Yes?

22:39.340 --> 22:42.420
"Following the footprints of the boy 
who moved ever forward,

22:42.420 --> 22:46.900
the fox senses the cold air of 
the deep woods on its whiskers

22:46.900 --> 22:48.680
and continues to wander.

22:49.380 --> 22:53.430
The human boy, too, continues 
to walk with no destination.

22:54.030 --> 22:56.750
They will both return to this place one day,

22:57.210 --> 23:00.230
in a never-ending cycle.

23:00.720 --> 23:03.990
'Forest spirit!' The fox calls out.

23:04.900 --> 23:09.750
'I've already lived for hundreds of years. 
I would like to rest soon.

23:10.270 --> 23:13.750
May I give this life of mine to that boy?'

23:14.580 --> 23:17.430
The branches of the trees all around shook."

23:17.430 --> 23:18.750
Ren-nii?

23:19.250 --> 23:22.540
The apartment wife wrote this book?

23:22.540 --> 23:23.770
That's right.

23:31.270 --> 23:34.160
Goodnight, Oto.

23:31.760 --> 23:35.020
<b>Simply Walk Alone,
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hLike a Rhino's Horn</b>

23:31.760 --> 23:35.020
<b>Winner of the Newcomer's Award</b>

23:31.760 --> 23:35.020
<b>Ogawa Sumireko</b>

23:35.020 --> 23:40.020
<b>A Bath, Cleaning, and a Surprise</b>

23:36.160 --> 23:39.980
Next time: "A Bath, Cleaning, and a Surprise."
